## Buying a refurbished HP laptop

HP's business laptops are a favourite with companies across India, and they make excellent refurbished buys. They tend to look polished, feel solid, and include security features that consumer laptops at the same price usually don't.

### Understanding HP's business range

- **EliteBook 800 series** — the most common premium business models. The **EliteBook 840** is a 14-inch all-rounder; the **830** is a more compact 13-inch option; the **850** offers a 15.6-inch screen.
- **EliteBook 1000 series and Dragonfly** — ultra-premium, lightweight models.
- **ProBook 400 series** — affordable business laptops such as the ProBook 440 and 450, ideal for office work and study on a budget.
- **ZBook** — mobile workstations with professional graphics for CAD, 3D and engineering software.

### The "G" number matters

HP labels each generation of a model with a "G" number — EliteBook 840 **G5**, **G6**, **G7** and so on. Newer generations usually bring newer processors, better screens and improved battery life. When comparing listings, check both the G number and the exact processor model.

### Features worth knowing about

Many HP business laptops include **HP Sure Start**, which helps protect the BIOS from tampering, and some are fitted with **Sure View**, a built-in privacy screen that makes the display hard to read from the side — useful when you work in public places. Fingerprint readers and webcam privacy shutters are common too.

### What to check before buying

1. Processor generation — 8th generation Intel or newer is a sensible minimum.
2. Screen resolution — look for Full HD (1920×1080).
3. Measured battery health, shown on every listing.
4. The [condition grade](/condition-grades) that fits your budget.

Each HP laptop goes through our [nine-step refurbishment process](/how-we-refurbish). Comparing brands? Read [Latitude vs ThinkPad vs EliteBook](/blog/best-business-laptops-for-professionals).
